  "narrative": {
   "care_continuity": [
    "National isolation/CTE stock: 738. The source prints no complete national capacity denominator.",
    "Ituri: 434 patients for 978 beds (44.4% occupancy); Nord-Kivu: 225 for 220 beds (102.7%, oversaturated); Haut-Uele: 62 for 128 beds (50.8%, 49 confirmed and 13 suspects); Tshopo: 6 for 25 beds (24.0%).",
    "Sud-Kivu and Bas-Uele publish no occupancy block; their values remain unset rather than inferred. The four published blocks sum to 727 against the printed national 738, an 11-patient residual left unallocated."
   ],
   "challenges": [
    "Alert volume fell 31.3% (2 610 to 1 792) and only five of six provinces reported: Sud-Kivu filed nothing. Verification also dropped to 84.4% (1 512/1 792) from 99.0% the cut before. Across five cuts the series has moved 2 445, 1 705, 2 610, 1 792 with no INSP correction to the completeness and time-window question SR109 raised, so it is not readable as a change in transmission.",
    "PoE/PoC report completeness is 86.3%, weakest at Sud-Kivu (55.5%) and Haut-Uele (64.0%); Bas-Uele filed ND. Only 1 of 11 (9.1%) strategic Ituri points runs without interruption.",
    "Contact follow-up improved to 88.5% (21 678/24 497) from 86.5%, but Bas-Uele at 69.6% (103/148) and Tshopo at 68.1% (241/354) remain well below the 85% threshold. Sud-Kivu publishes no contact row. INSP attributes the Bas-Uele weakness to insufficient dedicated teams.",
    "Care capacity: Nord-Kivu CTE/CT is oversaturated at 102.7% (225 patients, 220 beds).",
    "Two confirmed cases escaped custody this edition: one in Haut-Uele and one in Tshopo at day four of hospitalisation.",
    "Only four of six provinces publish an isolation block. Those four sum to 727 against the printed national 738, leaving an 11-patient unallocated residual that is preserved rather than distributed."
   ],
